# IntelliJ HTTP Client: provide local variables password, skuId and orderId.
# Put credentials in an untracked http-client.private.env.json, not this file.

### Warehouse identity
GET http://127.0.0.1:8082/api/auth/me
Authorization: Basic warehouse {{password}}

### Create a SKU
POST http://127.0.0.1:8082/api/skus
Authorization: Basic warehouse {{password}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"code":"MUG-001","name":"Demo mug","price":12.50}

### Receive stock; repeat the same key/content to verify idempotency
POST http://127.0.0.1:8082/api/inventory/{{skuId}}/receipts
Authorization: Basic warehouse {{password}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"operationKey":"receipt-001","quantity":10}

### Create an order; repeat this request to get the same order
POST http://127.0.0.1:8082/api/orders
Authorization: Basic buyer {{password}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"requestKey":"order-001","items":[{"skuId":{{skuId}},"quantity":2}]}

### Read own order
GET http://127.0.0.1:8082/api/orders/{{orderId}}
Authorization: Basic buyer {{password}}

### Confirm own order (simulated, no payment)
POST http://127.0.0.1:8082/api/orders/{{orderId}}/confirm
Authorization: Basic buyer {{password}}

### Cancel a pending own order
POST http://127.0.0.1:8082/api/orders/{{orderId}}/cancel
Authorization: Basic buyer {{password}}

### Warehouse fulfillment
GET http://127.0.0.1:8082/api/fulfillment/orders
Authorization: Basic warehouse {{password}}

### Ship a confirmed order
POST http://127.0.0.1:8082/api/fulfillment/orders/{{orderId}}/ship
Authorization: Basic warehouse {{password}}

### Buyer acknowledges receipt
POST http://127.0.0.1:8082/api/orders/{{orderId}}/complete
Authorization: Basic buyer {{password}}
